REDESIGN ONLY THE EXISTING “DOCUMENTATION & CONTACT” / “DOCUMENTATION” PAGE.

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT change the design, layout, typography, colours, navigation, footer, background, branding, or any other page of the existing Saath website.

The ONLY thing being changed is the CONTENT AND VISUAL PRESENTATION OF THE DOCUMENTATION SECTION.

The purpose of this page is to become a playful but credible DOCUMENTATION HUB for Saath.

It should feel like entering a physical archive of the organisation's work — using files, folders and books as visual metaphors — while still feeling mature, editorial, clean and trustworthy.

Do NOT make it look childish, cartoonish, like a school worksheet, or like a generic corporate document library.

The existing Saath visual identity must remain the foundation.

==================================================
PAGE PURPOSE
==================================================

The Documentation page should communicate:

“This is where the actual work behind Saath is documented.”

It should contain two primary categories:

1. CAMPAIGN DOCUMENTATION
2. CURRICULUM & LESSON PLANS

The page should be an ARCHIVE/HUB.

Do NOT put the full contents of every document directly onto this page.

Instead, visitors should interact with the visual document objects and open the corresponding document/page.

