==================================================
LAYOUT
==================================================

The page should have a strong visual hierarchy:

DOCUMENTATION
The work behind Saath.

↓

CAMPAIGN ARCHIVE
Campaigns, documented.

↓

[Large physical Campaign 01 file]

↓

CURRICULUM
What we teach.

↓

[Master Lesson Plan book]

↓

[Four subject books]

The layout should have generous whitespace.

Do not make everything perfectly symmetrical if a slightly organic editorial arrangement would better fit the existing Saath aesthetic.

However, maintain enough alignment and spacing that the page remains easy to navigate.

The physical objects can have very subtle differences in angle/position to make the page feel tactile.

Do NOT randomly scatter objects.

The layout must still feel intentional and professional.

==================================================
INTERACTIONS
==================================================

Every document object must clearly feel clickable.

Campaign 01 file:
→ Opens Campaign 01 page/report.

Master Lesson Plan:
→ Opens “Saath lesson plan”.

Digital Literacy book:
→ Opens “Lesson plan digital literacy, Hrithik”.

Financial Literacy book:
→ Opens “Lesson plan financial literacy, Jay”.

Sustainability book:
→ Opens “2. Sustainability block 1 lesson plan”.

Legal Literacy book:
→ Opens “Legal literacy Rhythm”.

Use subtle hover states.

For example:
- slight elevation
- slight movement
- very subtle shadow
- tiny change in rotation

Do NOT use:
- bouncing
- spinning
- large scaling
- flashy transitions
- confetti
- excessive animation

The interaction should feel like physically picking up/opening a document.

==================================================
DOCUMENT OPENING BEHAVIOUR
==================================================

IMPORTANT:

Do not create fake document content.

Do not fabricate missing information.

Do not rewrite the documents into summaries unless the existing website already requires a summary.

Where the actual document is available, the interaction should open the actual corresponding document/page.

If Figma Make cannot directly embed or open the supplied document files, create the visual interactive structure and use the appropriate document link/placeholder that can later be connected.

Do NOT pretend a document has been embedded if it has not.

==================================================
CREDIBILITY
==================================================

The visual design should balance:

PLAYFUL PRESENTATION
+
SERIOUS DOCUMENTATION

The physical files and books are visual metaphors.

The actual information must remain professional.

Do not make Saath look like a children's stationery brand.

The goal is:

“Young people built this, but they take the work seriously.”

==================================================
RESPONSIVE DESIGN
==================================================

On desktop:
- Keep the campaign file prominent.
- Display the curriculum books in a visually balanced arrangement.
- Keep the master lesson plan visually distinct.

On tablet:
- Allow the books to wrap naturally.

On mobile:
- Stack the documents vertically.
- Maintain clear labels and comfortable touch targets.
- Do not shrink the books so much that their labels become difficult to read.

Every document must remain easy to tap/click.

